# DIAGNOSTICS

The failures `dlerror` reports include: the file is not in bootfs; it is not a shared object; it has thread-local storage, which a loaded object cannot have; there was no room to map it; a relocation type is not supported; a symbol it needs is undefined.
For an undefined symbol the program must export its symbols, as a program built to host libraries does; the message says so otherwise.

# BUGS

Libraries come only from bootfs, not from the file system.
`dl_iterate_phdr` reports the program alone, not the libraries `dlopen` has loaded.
There are no `dladdr`, `dlinfo` or `dlvsym`, no lazy binding, no local scopes and no unloading.
